{
  "$schema": "../scene.schema.json",
  "id": "bellwater-priory",
  "name": "Bellwater Priory",
  "description": "Bead mw-e26.5 (with the priory legs of mw-e25.25): the ruined Vesperine monastery on the hill, a 120 x 130 m greybox. From the south edge (road-gate, back to the Briarwood's priory-road-gate; arrive-from-briarwood) the priory road runs north between a few trees to the precinct gate wall (priory-gate), past a forecourt into the roofless nave (priory-nave; walls and a colonnade, six metres tall, open to the sky). West of the nave: the garden with the dead pear tree (priory-garden, a dead end) and a sealed vestibule behind a locked door, the priory end of the cistern (cistern, cistern-door; the Glen Well route joins here in mw-e24.10 and mw-e26.20). North: the choir (priory-choir) with four singing-monk statue stubs and the altar for the Watchers puzzle (mw-e26.6) and, in its east wall, the hidden choir door (choir-hidden-door, locked, lock choir-door-hidden) to the scriptorium (scriptorium: shelves, book mimic, tallow ooze and abbot letter stubs, mw-e26.7). East: the belfry, a 9 m tower whose open doorway in the nave's east wall (belfry-stair-door, where mw-e26.8 fits the jammed door) leads up three stair flights to the deck, with the Sounding Shaft's mouth in the deck (sounding-shaft-top, vesper-bell above it), a rough-stone free-climb up the south face (belfry-climb-foot, grade 2) and two rope anchors on the south parapet (belfry-anchor-a/b); belfry-view is the perf viewpoint. East of the nave a stair descends 3 m to the crypt stair landing (priory-crypt-stair, the Sunbeam puzzle's place) and a locked tier-3 door (crypt-door, lock crypt-sealed) over the sealed crypt vestibule (priory-crypt): no route this side until world.priory-crypt.unsealed (mw-e26.20). The whole scene is the bellwater-priory region; the belfry volume is its own region.",
